1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:11,019
In rural Madagascar, one solar microgrid powers a
clinic, a school, water and every home.

2
00:00:11,019 --> 00:00:13,815
When the sun drops, who keeps the light?

3
00:00:13,815 --> 00:00:15,701
Mitsinjo Grid helps decide.

4
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:18,881
This village is fully simulated.

5
00:00:18,881 --> 00:00:24,732
I build a seven-day week: sun, clouds, then a storm,
with chaos mode for random incidents.

6
00:00:24,732 --> 00:00:31,819
Every setting is a lever: strategy, clinic lifeline floor,
night battery reserve, sector priorities and caps.

7
00:00:32,933 --> 00:00:35,436
We play the whole week in seconds, in
three views.

8
00:00:35,436 --> 00:00:38,090
The 3D scene shows the village through day
and night.

9
00:00:38,090 --> 00:00:41,344
The topology follows the power from the
solar hub to each sector.

10
00:00:41,344 --> 00:00:42,946
The circuit shows every breaker.

11
00:00:42,946 --> 00:00:46,050
Then the Strategy Lab: seventy percent
less sun for ten hours.

12
00:00:46,050 --> 00:00:51,707
Proportional sharing gives the clinic forty-four percent of its
energy; essential-first raises it to fifty-eight.

13
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:54,082
Who loses power first?

14
00:00:54,082 --> 00:00:55,655
I ask the copilot out loud.

15
00:00:55,655 --> 00:01:07,776
Muse Voice turns my speech into text, and Muse Spark answers by calling the engine's tools: homes, then the
clinic, fall short from the evening, and every number points to the simulation run that produced it.

16
00:01:08,867 --> 00:01:10,065
Now let the AI drive.

17
00:01:10,065 --> 00:01:20,447
In autonomous mode, the engine picks each action and applies it on its own, inside the village
rules: it shifts flexible loads, reserves the night battery, isolates a sector on fire.

18
00:01:20,447 --> 00:01:25,524
Muse Spark explains every decision in plain words,
checked against the engine's evidence.

19
00:01:25,524 --> 00:01:27,064
One tap takes back control.

20
00:01:28,167 --> 00:01:31,084
Second feature: real objects in the twin.

21
00:01:31,084 --> 00:01:32,151
I drop a photo.

22
00:01:32,151 --> 00:01:40,190
Muse Spark names the appliances and buildings, and SAM 3.1
outlines each one, marked as AI perception, to verify.

23
00:01:40,190 --> 00:01:41,470
Missing something?

24
00:01:41,470 --> 00:01:43,889
I draw it with the magnetic lasso.

25
00:01:45,033 --> 00:01:46,149
I pick a building.

26
00:01:46,149 --> 00:01:48,691
Muse Image draws a clean front elevation.

27
00:01:48,691 --> 00:01:50,862
I add details, retry, and validate.

28
00:01:50,862 --> 00:01:58,798
Muse Spark then builds the 3D model piece by piece: massing, roof,
openings, accessories, each stage scored against the drawing.

29
00:01:58,798 --> 00:02:01,588
Then I turn the model, resize it and tint
it.

30
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:07,655
Then its load: an AI estimate or my own
watts, with the twenty-four-hour curve.

31
00:02:07,655 --> 00:02:11,481
I place it on the map, choose its feeder
line, and insert it.

32
00:02:11,481 --> 00:02:17,377
The model now stands in the 3D village, and every
strategy is recomputed with its consumption.

33
00:02:18,467 --> 00:02:25,319
Four Meta models, one job each: Voice listens, Spark
reasons and builds, SAM outlines, Image draws.

34
00:02:25,319 --> 00:02:31,480
A deterministic engine behind every number, and a
human who can always take back control.

35
00:02:32,567 --> 00:02:33,549
Mitsinjo Grid.

36
00:02:33,549 --> 00:02:35,724
Simulated data, real decisions.

